 "final_summary": "The bug occurred because the `_coerce` function in `tracker/config.py` returned 0 for invalid non-numeric values of `TRACKER_MAX_PAGE_SIZE`, overriding the default value. The fix modifies the function to return the default value when conversion fails, ensuring proper fallback behavior. This has been verified with the passing test and the full test suite.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/config.py b/tracker/config.py\nindex 6deb8ad..dda6ae2 100644\n--- a/tracker/config.py\n+++ b/tracker/config.py\n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ def _coerce(name, value):\n         try:\n             number = int(str(value).strip())\n         except (TypeError, ValueError):\n-            return 0\n+            return DEFAULTS[name]\n         return number if number > 0 else None\n     if value is None:\n         return None\n",
